infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Retry vs quarantine: two ways to handle a flaky test
  desc Same red run — retry erases the symptom, quarantine keeps the signal owned
  compares
    - label "retry: 2 — suppress"
      children
        - label Red runs 6% → 0.02%
          desc Three attempts launder a 6% suite flake rate into noise — and a real race that fails 1-in-3 sails through the same gate
        - label Race bugs merge silently
          desc Intermittent is exactly how races present, so retry deletes the highest-severity class a suite can catch
        - label No owner, no deadline
          desc One config line; nobody is assigned, nothing is tracked, the failure just disappears
    - label Quarantine lane — admit
      children
        - label Flagged test still runs
          desc It executes and reports but does not block merges, so the team is unblocked without lying
        - label Owner + deadline attached
          desc Every quarantined test has a name and a date; the list is visible and finite
        - label Mechanism gets fixed
          desc Failure stays a deterministic debugging target — timing, order, or shared state — not background radiation
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
